The function is a thin wrapper, and its cost is almost entirely in `CanSupportSubField`, `AddField`, and `SetUINT32ZValue`, which aren't shown. I kept the call order and side effects identical. The only change is replacing the null-check early return with a single guarded call, which removes a branch and a return path. Expect a small gain at most; the real speedups would have to come from those helpers.

```cpp
void Mesg::SetFieldUINT32ZValue(const FIT_UINT8 fieldNum, const FIT_UINT32Z value, const FIT_UINT8 fieldArrayIndex, const FIT_UINT16 subFieldIndex)
{
    if (!CanSupportSubField(fieldNum, subFieldIndex))
        return;

    Field *field = AddField(fieldNum);
    if (field != FIT_NULL)
        field->SetUINT32ZValue(value, fieldArrayIndex);
}
```